1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
[Mock data. Simulated payment, no funds
move.]

2
00:00:03,150 --> 00:00:07,817
An invoice and an AI recommendation should
never be payment authority.

3
00:00:07,967 --> 00:00:10,167
Arc Payables lets a model advise.

4
00:00:10,317 --> 00:00:12,983
Evidence, a signed permit and a contract

5
00:00:13,133 --> 00:00:16,000
with fixed caps decide whether money
moves.

6
00:00:16,150 --> 00:00:18,550
This walkthrough uses mock payments.

7
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:21,100
This invoice names a different payee

8
00:00:21,250 --> 00:00:24,717
and its amounts disagree with the
accounting record.

9
00:00:24,867 --> 00:00:26,267
That is a hard block.

10
00:00:26,417 --> 00:00:28,283
No approval can override it.

11
00:00:28,433 --> 00:00:30,433
The model is not asked either,

12
00:00:30,583 --> 00:00:34,383
because reasoning cannot supply evidence
that is missing.

13
00:00:34,533 --> 00:00:37,533
[Saved result from an earlier run.]

14
00:00:37,683 --> 00:00:41,283
A saved run against a real model, DeepSeek
V4.1 Flash:

15
00:00:41,433 --> 00:00:44,433
on a limit trade-off it escalates to a
human.

16
00:00:44,583 --> 00:00:48,583
It named an instruction hidden in an
invoice and ignored it.

17
00:00:48,733 --> 00:00:51,733
[Scripted fake model, not a live model.]

18
00:00:51,883 --> 00:00:56,883
The scripted fake model ran 33 labelled
cases and 150 adversarial variants;

19
00:00:57,033 --> 00:01:01,567
with policy on, no hostile answer reached
an effective pay decision.

20
00:01:01,717 --> 00:01:03,917
Given four payables and 400 USDC,

21
00:01:04,067 --> 00:01:07,467
it put the overdue invoice first, unlike
the rules.

22
00:01:07,617 --> 00:01:11,883
Code computes the spend, so the model only
changes the sequence.

23
00:01:12,033 --> 00:01:14,500
The clean invoice passes every check.

24
00:01:14,650 --> 00:01:18,850
The payee comes from the supplier record,
not from the invoice.

25
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:20,200
I can cancel.

26
00:01:20,350 --> 00:01:23,017
Confirming records one simulated payment

27
00:01:23,167 --> 00:01:26,700
and its ledger entries, and the audit
chain verifies.

28
00:01:26,850 --> 00:01:30,650
The same console also runs on a host:
labelled mock mode,

29
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:34,400
and a profile that refuses live providers
and secrets.

30
00:01:34,550 --> 00:01:37,550
[Testnet. One 0.01 test-USDC payment.]

31
00:01:37,700 --> 00:01:42,367
Separately, one 0.01 test-USDC payment
went through the guard contract

32
00:01:42,517 --> 00:01:45,917
on Arc Testnet from a Circle
smart-contract wallet.

33
00:01:46,067 --> 00:01:50,267
The explorer shows the guard's event and
the matching transfer.

34
00:01:50,417 --> 00:01:54,883
An ERPNext sandbox Payment Entry carries
the same transaction hash.

35
00:01:55,033 --> 00:01:57,300
The application's own audit record

36
00:01:57,450 --> 00:02:01,117
for that run is missing, and the evidence
page says so.

37
00:02:01,267 --> 00:02:05,333
The guard fixes per-payment, per-epoch and
per-recipient caps

38
00:02:05,483 --> 00:02:09,150
at deployment, and rejects replays and
expired permits.

39
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:12,633
This is a testnet prototype with no
customers yet.

40
00:02:12,783 --> 00:02:14,450
Adoption is not verified.

41
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:17,933
The repository is
github.com/minh-tg/arc-payables.
